# Rigor core overlay — supplemental core signatures.
#
# --- MatchData#integer_at (Ruby 4.1) ---
#
# Issue #1691. Ruby 4.1 adds `MatchData#integer_at` (`re.c`, call-seq
# `integer_at(index, base = 10) -> integer or nil` and
# `integer_at(name, base = 10) -> integer or nil`): `$~.integer_at(N)` is
# `$N&.to_i`. No rbs release through 4.2 declares it, so correct 4.1 code
# reported `call.undefined-method`. A non-Integer first argument is read as
# a group name; `base` goes through `NUM2INT`, hence `int`.
#
# TEMPORARY: delete this file once the rbs release Rigor bundles declares
# the method upstream.
#
# Declared unconditionally, not gated on `target_ruby` (ADR-121 § Rejected
# alternatives; false positives outrank), and on a module `MatchData`
# includes so that a later direct declaration overrides it instead of
# raising `DuplicatedMethodDefinitionError` for the whole class (see
# `process.rbs`).
module RigorCoreOverlay
  module Ruby41MatchData
    def integer_at: (Integer | String | Symbol index_or_name, ?int base) -> Integer?
  end
end

class MatchData
  include RigorCoreOverlay::Ruby41MatchData
end
